592186045417] [17592186297131 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297131 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186295760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297131 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f48c190e-f08c-555e-ba42-c4bbbf078a30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297306 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297306 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297306 #edb/ref 1069 "q-308823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297306 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297306 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{2}{x}+1$ at the point $(1,3)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297306 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ac03aacc-0b7e-5a7f-8554-ee3b669a879c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297306 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{x}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-1}+1) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=-\\frac{2}{(1)^{2}}=-2,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the  $x$-axis at $(\\,-5,0\\,).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480110 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092384.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480110 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "5a713bd5-e4da-55c7-a366-7eebf361a0e5" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493312 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $f(x)=10 x^{2} + 5 x$ at the point $(1,15)$ intersects the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e3f1a4a-bfde-54af-80e2-4cc4e890e6fc" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 x^{2} + 5 x)=20 x + 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=25=25,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(25)}=- \\frac{1}{25}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(15)&=- \\frac{1}{25}(x-(1))\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x-(- \\frac{1}{25})+(15)\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}&=0\\\\x&=376.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(376,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493309 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493319 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{20}{x}+10$ at the point $(1,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c1268dd-9a0b-5590-983e-596506fe3286" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\frac{20}{x}+10)\\\\&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 + \\frac{20}{x})\\\\&=-20x^{-2}\\\\&=- \\frac{20}{x^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=-20=-20,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-20)}=\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{20}(x-(1))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x-(\\frac{1}{20})+(30)\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}&=0\\\\x&=-599.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the  $x$-axis at $(-599,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493315 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493323 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30$ at the point $(0,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3c9763c-f1e1-51a2-887f-38a4a610161d" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30)=36 x - 36.\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(0)=-36=-36,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-36)}=\\frac{1}{36}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{36}(x-(0))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{36}x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{36}x+30&=0\\\\\\frac{1}{36}x&=-30\\\\x&=-1080.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(-1080,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493324 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092385.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493324 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "6f93f05c-93ce-5432-b4e0-7ec958ee8e90" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493326 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092240.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493326 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "733357e0-41a3-5401-bdd5-4100649b68a2" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186547100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186547118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186547159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating the Equation of a Normal Line Using Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186547100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546252 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "fad01a8c-be82-5d4b-b516-bfef7fe94dc5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546543 #edb/ref 1080 "-13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546543 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546543 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "85168c9f-eca2-5f20-86c3-38ab8f99e07f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546771 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546771 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546771 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e827c707-4183-5bda-8490-ae6373ae9ace" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546911 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546911 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #e